# =====================================================================
# Noesis SBOM — Trivy Ignore Policy (v0.2.0-rc2, MS9 deliverable)
# =====================================================================
# Policy: 0 HIGH / 0 CRITICAL vulnerabilities allowed in release images.
#
# This file is intentionally EMPTY.  Every HIGH or CRITICAL finding from
# `trivy image` MUST be triaged and fixed (base-image rebuild, pinning a
# patched transitive wheel, or removing the vulnerable dependency).
#
# If — and only if — a finding is a PROVEN FALSE POSITIVE (Trivy CPE
# mismatch against a Python package name, or a distro package that we
# explicitly do not use at runtime), add a single ignore block below
# with:
#   1. CVE id
#   2. Exact reason + false-positive proof (link to upstream issue, or
#      a `docker run --rm … rpm -ql / dpkg -L` transcript proving the
#      binary / library is not present in the final runtime layer).
#   3. Expiry date: MUST be <= 30 days so the exemption is revisited on
#      every RC cut.
#
# Template:
#   # CVE-YYYY-NNNNN: False positive — CPE match against <pkg-name> when
#   # actual installed package is <other-name>. Proof: <link or SHA>.
#   # Expires: YYYY-MM-DD
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN
#
# Audit log (kept empty by policy for v0.2.0-rc2):
#   (none)
# =====================================================================
